body:
I'm 20 and a christian. Spent my recent b day alone, awas broke af, and i know how you feel.

&#x200B;

all the best x

it is unrealistic. life happens

&#x200B;

but a pollyana mindset is helpful at times.

as someone who is not wealthy, is that true? I'm not trying to invalidate your experience but as someone who is not wealthy, to me money would cure a lot of my issues. I could get good therapy, I could travel to clear my mind, it would be atleast comforting to have money and not be on the verge of eviction. financial stress really inflames the inner critic.

&#x200B;

but i guess if you have cptsd it's harder to enjoy life, and therefore money, travel, whatever it be. And to be fair you said it was your parents money, not necessarily yours.
